---
import Prose from '../../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { getDocsPage } from '../../data/docs-topics';

const page = getDocsPage('config');
---
<Prose title={page.title} description={page.description} path={page.path}>
  <p>Every setting except the API key, the file types and the terminal command is also in <code>config.toml</code> in Jotra's data folder, <code>~/.jotra</code>, or <code>~/.writ</code> on a computer that ran Writ, including which programs you approved. Logs are in its <code>logs</code> folder. Jotra checks for an update shortly after launch, at most once a day, and Settings, About turns the check off.</p>
  <p><code>[files] image_folder</code> is where pasted and dropped images are saved, relative to the Markdown file's folder: <code>assets</code> when it is not set, and beside the file when it is empty. <code>[editor] load_remote_images = true</code> loads images from web addresses in Inline mode without a click.</p>
  <p><code>[dictation]</code> holds <code>enabled</code>, <code>engine</code> (<code>"api"</code> or <code>"on_device"</code>; without it, On this Mac where the Mac supports it and API elsewhere), <code>provider</code> (<code>"openai"</code>, <code>"groq"</code> or <code>"custom"</code>), <code>base_url</code> for a custom server, <code>model</code>, <code>language</code> (an ISO 639-1 code such as <code>"en"</code>, or empty for Automatic) and <code>clean_up</code>. Jotra writes <code>consented_hosts</code>, the hosts you allowed to receive audio.</p>
</Prose>
